          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For measuring temperature, the clinical thermometers generally use a scale called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Celsius scale",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". On this scale, the unit of temperature is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "degree Celsius",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and is denoted by °C."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.262,
            0.795,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Earlier, mercury thermometers were used for measuring the body temperature. But mercury is an extremely toxic substance and is difficult to dispose of if the thermometer breaks accidently."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.348,
            0.738,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
